These files should give a good idea of what needs to happen in order to make sockets work.
They are not intended to be actually used, though you can attempt to use them if you want.  I think the "Another...c" files actually have a few minor compile errors that need to be ironed out.

The main focus for the tablet-based API should be on:
  1.  Automatically finding the IP address of the Raspberry Pi.
  2.  Connecting to the Raspberry Pi.
  3.  Sending a message to the Raspberry Pi. (could be the name of the program that turns the lamp on or off)
